  designNotes: "Beat 9: tension inverted. Default is 6 rifle + 2 shield \u2014 they
    take half damage and still fire, so the outnumbered line has bodies that stay up.
    Twenty-two against ten, six of them advancing,
    so for the first time the player is losing on arithmetic and has to win on concentration.
    Win condition is unchanged (roster), which is the point \u2014 it FEELS like
    a defence without being a different game. Two wire props, both slowing, because
    at this count an unslowed charge arrives before the third volley. Structure hp
    RETUNED 2026-08-07: bunker and barracks both hpScale 0.7 (180 -> 126, 150 ->
    105), garrisoned total 330 -> 229. Measured on device at 330: THREE runs, three
    total defeats - once the three tank shells were spent the squad did about 8 structure
    damage a volley while losing about one unit a volley, so the 13 garrisoned enemies
    could never be reached. Enemy roster CUT 22 -> 15 on 2026-08-07 (shields 6->4,
    forward rifles 3->2, bunker gunners 5->3, barracks rifles 8->6). Two reasons.
    It fielded 22 against the player's 10, the widest body ratio in the campaign,
    and a 22-body line out-shoots a 10-body line every turn however the walls are
    tuned - the volley race flagged this level worst at 4.1x. And the garrisons were
    over the decks they stand on: LEVEL_AUTHORING's capacity table rates a MountainBunker
    at ~2 and a BarracksBlock at ~4, and this level had 5 and 8 on them. Garrison
    stays the majority at 9 of 15."
